description:
Found by s501t (s505) probing F1's siblings.  Pre-existing on main a33ce274 (scalar tie, not the s501t aggregate tie).

Reproducer (perl prints `A a3`):
  require Tie::Scalar; package A; sub new { bless [$_[1]], $_[0] } sub m { "a" . $_[0][0] } package main;
  tie my $s, 'Tie::StdScalar'; $s = A->new(3); print ref($s), " ", $s->m, "\n";
PCL: ref is "" and the method call dies "Can't locate object method m via package main".  A blessed HASH works (its class lives in the table); an ARRAY's class lives on the reference's wrapper box, which the tie-proxy's unbox peels away.  The s501t element proxy solved the same thing for tied ARRAY/HASH elements by copying the wrapper's class onto the proxy box (%p-tie-elem-value) and reading ref() / the invocant class through the wrapper -- the scalar proxy wants the same.
